IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pip-nouns`

-- SCHEDULE 1, PART 1 -- INTERPRETATION (paragraph 1): the words the descriptors use.
--
-- Each definition is a rule over plain facts: whether a thing is "assistance", "supervision",
-- "a simple meal" and so on. The descriptors of Parts 2 and 3 are data (the table modules);
-- these definitions are what a person (or an officer) reads to decide whether a descriptor is
-- satisfied, so they are encoded as tests, one rule for each defined term.
--
-- How the lists were read (fork F-12 in NOTES.md): where a definition lists parts joined by
-- "and" (complex budgeting decisions, simple budgeting decisions, engage socially, toilet
-- needs, take nutrition (a), manage incontinence), the list is the set of parts that make up
-- the defined term, so a thing is within the term if it is any one of them. Where a
-- definition lists conditions ("where a failure to do so is likely to result in a
-- deterioration", "without which C's health is likely to deteriorate"), the conditions are
-- cumulative.

§ `Schedule 1, Part 1: interpretation`

-- "aided" means with (a) the use of an aid or appliance; or (b) supervision, prompting or assistance.
-- src:498 | “aided” means with –
-- src:499 | (a) the use of an aid or appliance; or
-- src:500 | (b) supervision, prompting or assistance;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "aided" (src:498-500)
GIVEN `C uses an aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has prompting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: C does the activity aided` MEANS
        `C uses an aid or appliance`
     OR (   `C has supervision`
         OR `C has prompting`
         OR `C has assistance`)

-- "unaided" means without (a) the use of an aid or appliance; or (b) supervision, prompting or assistance.
-- src:562 | “unaided” means without –
-- src:563 | (a) the use of an aid or appliance; or
-- src:564 | (b) supervision, prompting or assistance.
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "unaided" (src:562-564)
GIVEN `C uses an aid or appliance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has prompting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `C has assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: C does the activity unaided` MEANS
        (NOT `C uses an aid or appliance`)
    AND (NOT (   `C has supervision`
              OR `C has prompting`
              OR `C has assistance`))

-- "assistance" means physical intervention by another person and does not include speech.
-- src:501 | “assistance” means physical intervention by another person and does not include speech;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "assistance" (src:501)
GIVEN `it is physical intervention by another person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is speech` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is assistance` MEANS
        `it is physical intervention by another person`
    AND (NOT `it is speech`)

-- "assistance dog" means a dog trained to guide or assist a person with a sensory impairment.
-- src:502 | “assistance dog” means a dog trained to guide or assist a person with a sensory impairment;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "assistance dog" (src:502)
GIVEN `it is a dog` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is trained to guide or assist a person with a sensory impairment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is an assistance dog` MEANS
        `it is a dog`
    AND `it is trained to guide or assist a person with a sensory impairment`

-- "basic verbal information" means information in C's native language conveyed verbally in a simple sentence.
-- src:503 | “basic verbal information” means information in C's native language conveyed verbally in a simple sentence;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "basic verbal information" (src:503)
GIVEN `it is in C's native language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conveyed verbally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in a simple sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is basic verbal information` MEANS
        `it is in C's native language`
    AND `it is conveyed verbally`
    AND `it is in a simple sentence`

-- "basic written information" means signs, symbols and dates written or printed standard size
-- text in C's native language. Signs, symbols and dates are the kinds of thing the information
-- may be (F-12).
-- src:504 | “basic written information” means signs, symbols and dates written or printed standard size text in C's native language;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "basic written information" (src:504)
GIVEN `it is signs, symbols or dates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is written or printed in standard size text` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in C's native language` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is basic written information` MEANS
        `it is signs, symbols or dates`
    AND `it is written or printed in standard size text`
    AND `it is in C's native language`

-- "bathe" includes get into or out of an unadapted bath or shower.
-- src:505 | “bathe” includes get into or out of an unadapted bath or shower;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "bathe" (src:505)
GIVEN `it is bathing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is getting into or out of an unadapted bath or shower` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is bathing` MEANS
       `it is bathing`
    OR `it is getting into or out of an unadapted bath or shower`

-- "communication support" means support from a person trained or experienced in communicating
-- with people with specific communication needs, including interpreting verbal information into
-- a non-verbal form and vice versa. The "including" gives an example of such support: interpreting
-- is communication support when it comes from such a person, and needs no further condition.
-- src:506 | “communication support” means support from a person trained or experienced in communicating with people with specific communication needs, including interpreting verbal information into a non-verbal form and vice versa;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "communication support" (src:506)
GIVEN `it is support from a person trained or experienced in communicating with people with specific communication needs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is communication support` MEANS
    `it is support from a person trained or experienced in communicating with people with specific communication needs`

-- "complex budgeting decisions" means decisions involving (a) calculating household and personal
-- budgets; (b) managing and paying bills; and (c) planning future purchases.
-- src:507 | “complex budgeting decisions” means decisions involving –
-- src:508 | (a) calculating household and personal budgets;
-- src:509 | (b) managing and paying bills; and
-- src:510 | (c) planning future purchases;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "complex budgeting decisions" (src:507-510)
GIVEN `it involves calculating household and personal budgets` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves managing and paying bills` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it involves planning future purchases` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is a complex budgeting decision` MEANS
       `it involves calculating household and personal budgets`
    OR `it involves managing and paying bills`
    OR `it involves planning future purchases`

-- "complex verbal information" means information in C's native language conveyed verbally in
-- either more than one sentence or one complicated sentence.
-- src:511 | “complex verbal information” means information in C's native language conveyed verbally in either more than one sentence or one complicated sentence;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "complex verbal information" (src:511)
GIVEN `it is in C's native language` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conveyed verbally` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in more than one sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in one complicated sentence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is complex verbal information` MEANS
        `it is in C's native language`
    AND `it is conveyed verbally`
    AND (   `it is in more than one sentence`
         OR `it is in one complicated sentence`)

-- "complex written information" means more than one sentence of written or printed standard size
