-- "take nutrition" means (a) cut food into pieces, convey food and drink to one's mouth and chew and
-- swallow food and drink; or (b) take nutrition by using a therapeutic source.
-- src:546 | “take nutrition” means –
-- src:547 | (a) cut food into pieces, convey food and drink to one's mouth and chew and swallow food and drink; or
-- src:548 | (b) take nutrition by using a therapeutic source;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "take nutrition" (src:546-548)
GIVEN `it is cutting food into pieces` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is conveying food and drink to one's mouth` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is chewing and swallowing food and drink` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is taking nutrition by using a therapeutic source` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is taking nutrition` MEANS
        (   `it is cutting food into pieces`
         OR `it is conveying food and drink to one's mouth`
         OR `it is chewing and swallowing food and drink`)
     OR `it is taking nutrition by using a therapeutic source`

-- "therapeutic source" means parenteral or enteral tube feeding, using a rate-limiting device such as a
-- delivery system or feed pump.
-- src:549 | “therapeutic source” means parenteral or enteral tube feeding, using a rate-limiting device such as a delivery system or feed pump;
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "therapeutic source" (src:549)
GIVEN `it is parenteral or enteral tube feeding` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it uses a rate-limiting device such as a delivery system or feed pump` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is a therapeutic source` MEANS
        `it is parenteral or enteral tube feeding`
    AND `it uses a rate-limiting device such as a delivery system or feed pump`

-- "therapy" means therapy to be undertaken at home which is prescribed or recommended by a (a) registered
-- (i) doctor; (ii) nurse; (iii) pharmacist; or (iv) physician associate; or (b) health professional
-- regulated by the Health Professions Council; but does not include taking or applying, or otherwise
-- receiving or administering, medication (whether orally, topically or by any other means), or any action
-- which, in C's case, falls within the definition of "monitor a health condition".
-- src:550 | “therapy” means therapy to be undertaken at home which is prescribed or recommended by a—
-- src:551 | (a) registered –
-- src:552 | (i) doctor;
-- src:553 | (ii) nurse; ...
-- src:554 | (iii) pharmacist; or
-- src:555 | (iv) a physician associate; or
-- src:556 | (b) health professional regulated by the Health Professions Council;
-- src:557 | but does not include taking or applying, or otherwise receiving or administering, medication (whether orally, topically or by any other means), or any action which, in C’s case, falls within the definition of “monitor a health condition
@ref Schedule 1, Part 1, para 1 "therapy" (src:550-557)
GIVEN `it is to be undertaken at home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered doctor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered nurse` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered physician associate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is prescribed or recommended by a health professional regulated by the Health Professions Council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is taking, applying, receiving or administering medication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in C's case it is an action within the definition of monitor a health condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Sch 1 para 1: this is therapy` MEANS
        `it is to be undertaken at home`
    AND (   `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered doctor`
         OR `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered nurse`
         OR `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered pharmacist`
         OR `it is prescribed or recommended by a registered physician associate`
         OR `it is prescribed or recommended by a health professional regulated by the Health Professions Council`)
    AND (NOT `it is taking, applying, receiving or administering medication`)
    AND (NOT `in C's case it is an action within the definition of monitor a health condition`)

-- "toilet needs" means (a) getting on and off an unadapted toilet; (b) evacuating the bladder and bowel;
